; The console wire protocol — the one seam between a console FRONTEND (the terminal driver, or a
; future web/editor surface) and the in-server eval ENGINE. Deliberately tiny and dependency-light
; (stdlib + the test runner only) so any frontend can speak it without pulling the framework or the
; compiler. The message TYPES are the contract; both ends Marshal them, so no hand-written serializer
; can ever drift from the types (the robustness the OCaml type system buys us for free).
(library
 (name console_protocol)
 (public_name fennec.console.protocol)
 (libraries fennec-hunt.unit)
 (inline_tests
  (backend fennec-hunt.runner))
 (preprocess
  (pps fennec-hunt.ppx)))
